  "interpretation": [
    "Temporal features had higher AUROC and average precision than static features on set B across all three exploratory seeds.",
    "Validation-only Platt recalibration substantially lowered Brier score and log loss on set B across all three splits while leaving ranking metrics effectively unchanged.",
    "This is evidence for a promising calibration experiment, not proof of clinically valid or transportable risk probabilities. Set A validation prevalence was about 2.17%, while set B prevalence was 1.415%.",
    "Reported standard deviations are across three seeds, not confidence intervals."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "Both cohorts are from the same PhysioNet/CinC Challenge 2019 benchmark, not prospective clinical validation.",
    "Hourly challenge-label metrics are not patient-level event sensitivity, lead time, or real-world clinical false-alarm rates.",
    "The threshold 0.5 is not clinically selected.",
    "Exact checked-in source-byte identity has not been verified; local harness was reconstructed.",
    "No raw patient records, identifiers, or row-level predictions are included."
  ]
